# FCS league server settings.
# Installed as /etc/fcs-league/league.env (readable by everyone on the server: NO SECRETS IN THIS FILE).
# The two tokens go in /etc/fcs-league/registry.env and /etc/fcs-league/bridge.env, which only root can read.
#
# Format: NAME=value, one per line, no quotes, no spaces around "=". Lines starting with # are notes.
# Do NOT put a note after a value on the same line. "NCAA_CLOUD=1 # public" is read as the value "1 # public".
# The server refuses to start on a value like that and the log says which setting is wrong.
# On/off settings take: on, 1, true, yes / off, 0, false, no. Anything else stops the server with a clear message.
# After a change:  sudo systemctl restart fcs-league.target

# ---- required ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Turns on the public-server profile. The server then refuses to start without a player registry, tells consoles to
# use NCAA_PUBLIC_HOST, limits connections and logins, and keeps passwords, credentials and packet bodies out of logs.
# This line must be exactly as it is. Without it the server would let anyone sign in, so it also refuses to listen
# on a public address when this is off. check.sh confirms from the log that cloud mode is really on.
NCAA_CLOUD=1

# The public name (or IPv4 address) of this server. Consoles are told to connect here.
# Point a DNS "A" record at the server first ("DNS only", not proxied through Cloudflare).
NCAA_PUBLIC_HOST=play.fcs-mod.online

# The companion website. The player registry, Supersim results and the site sync all use it. Must be https.
# (NCAA_SITE_URL is accepted as another name for the same setting.)
NCAA_WORKER_URL=https://fcs-mod.online

# ---- where things live (set by provision.sh; change only if you move folders) -----------------------------------

# League data: dynasties, uploaded saves, the cached registry. Back this folder up (backup.sh does, daily).
NCAA_PRIVATE=/var/lib/fcs-league/private
# The same folder, under the name the site sync (ncaa-bridge od watch) reads.
NCAA_OD_DIR=/var/lib/fcs-league/private
# The redirector's certificate and key (gosredirector_mod.crt, gosredirector.key.pem).
NCAA_CERT_DIR=/etc/fcs-league/certs

# ---- optional: how consoles are told the address ----------------------------------------------------------------

# ip    (default) the server looks up NCAA_PUBLIC_HOST itself and sends consoles the IPv4 address. This is the form
#       the game is proven to accept. A DNS change is picked up within five minutes, no restart needed.
# host  send the hostname itself where the game takes text (redirector reply, QoS site, Locker links). Untested with
#       a real console; only try it if "ip" gives trouble.
#NCAA_ADVERTISE=ip

# ---- optional: player registry ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# How often (seconds) the registry is pulled from the site. A player disabled on the site is disconnected within
# this time. If the site cannot be reached the last good copy keeps working.
#NCAA_REGISTRY_INTERVAL=60

# If the site cannot be reached for a long time, the copy gets old. Someone you disabled on the site could still
# sign in with the old copy. So:
#   after WARN hours the log has a WARNING line, once an hour (check.sh shows it);
#   after MAX_AGE hours nobody NEW can sign in until the site answers again. People already playing keep playing.
# The defaults ride out a site outage of three days. 0 = never warn / never stop.
#NCAA_REGISTRY_WARN_HOURS=6
#NCAA_REGISTRY_MAX_AGE_HOURS=72

# Lowest user id the site may hand out. Ids below this are reserved for accounts set up by hand, so a site bug can
# never take over one of those. A registry naming a lower id is refused as a whole.
#NCAA_REGISTRY_MIN_USER_ID=800000

# Where the registry is cached. Default: $NCAA_PRIVATE/league-registry.json
#NCAA_REGISTRY_FILE=/var/lib/fcs-league/private/league-registry.json

# off = do not sync; use only the file above, edited by hand (league-enroll.mjs). The server still refuses to start
# without a valid file.
#NCAA_REGISTRY_SYNC=on

# ---- optional: features -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# In-game Dynasty Wire (EA Sports World). On by default. Leave it on: with it off the game shows "You have lost
# your connection to EA servers" pop-ups while saving. Its signed-in mode was proven with the game on 2026-11-16.
# It uses port 17504/tcp, which firewall.sh opens unless this is set to off.
#NCAA_EASW=on

# Web-simulated games (Supersim) from the site. on by default, but on this server it only works when the game
# service has the full bridge token (see registry.env and "The two tokens" in the README). Without it the log says
# "web-simulated games are not polled" and nothing else changes.
#NCAA_SUPERSIM=on

# How long (seconds) a dynasty stays locked when someone starts saving to it and never finishes. After this the lock
# is dropped by itself. It is also dropped when that player disconnects.
#NCAA_UPDATE_LOCK_SECONDS=300

# ---- optional: ports (the game expects the defaults; change only for testing) ------------------------------------
#NCAA_REDIRECTOR_PORT=42127
#NCAA_BLAZE_PORT=33152
#NCAA_LOCKER_PORT=17503
#NCAA_EASW_PORT=17504
#NCAA_QOS_PORT=17502
#NCAA_QOS_FW1=17500
#NCAA_QOS_FW2=17501
# Address to listen on. 0.0.0.0 = every IPv4 address of this server (the default in cloud mode).
# Must be an IP address. Without cloud mode the server only listens on 127.0.0.1 unless NCAA_LAN=on says the
# network is a trusted home network. Never set NCAA_LAN on a public server.
#NCAA_BIND=0.0.0.0

# ---- optional: limits (defaults shown) ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Open connections: in total, and from one address (people behind one router share an address).
#NCAA_MAX_CONNS=2000
#NCAA_MAX_CONNS_PER_IP=16
# New connections per minute from one address.
#NCAA_CONNS_PER_MIN_PER_IP=120
# Failed logins per minute from one address before it is refused.
#NCAA_LOGIN_ATTEMPTS_PER_MIN=10
# Seconds a connection may stay without logging in, and without sending anything.
#NCAA_PREAUTH_SECONDS=120
#NCAA_IDLE_SECONDS=300
# Packets one connection may send in ten seconds.
#NCAA_PACKETS_PER_10S=5000
# Packet sizes on the game port:
#   before sign-in (KB). A real console sends at most about half a KB here.
#   after sign-in, ordinary commands (KB).
#   after sign-in, the commands that upload table rows (MB). The largest real one is 0.2 MB.
#NCAA_PREAUTH_PACKET_KB=4
#NCAA_COMMAND_PACKET_KB=64
#NCAA_MAX_PACKET_MB=4
# Largest uploaded file (MB), storage per player (MB), files per player.
# Files a player deleted are kept for 14 days and count toward the same storage; the oldest go first when room is needed.
#NCAA_MAX_UPLOAD_MB=32
#NCAA_LOCKER_QUOTA_MB=512
#NCAA_LOCKER_MAX_ITEMS=500
# Dynasties one player may have created that still exist. Leaving a dynasty to someone else does not free a slot.
#NCAA_MAX_DYNASTIES_PER_USER=10

# ---- optional: storage limits (defaults shown) ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# These stop one player, or everyone together, from filling the disk. They are on for this server.
# When a limit is reached the upload is refused, the game shows an error, and the log has a line starting with
# "REFUSED (storage limit)" that names the limit. Nothing already stored is lost.
# For scale: a normal dynasty is about 85 tables and 19 MB of tables. Its biggest table has 11,300 rows and is 9.5 MB.
# With its save files a dynasty takes about 55 MB in all.
#
# The budget for ALL league data (MB): dynasties, tables, saves, game data. When it is full, new uploads are refused
# and the log says "STORAGE FULL". 2048 is room for about 35 dynasties.
# The daily backups are on the same disk, and 14 are kept. Each can be as large as the data.
# So do not raise this without a bigger disk: 2048 suits a 20 GB disk, 4096 a 40 GB disk.
#NCAA_STATE_BUDGET_MB=2048
# One table: most rows, and largest size (MB).
#NCAA_TABLE_MAX_ROWS=60000
#NCAA_TABLE_MAX_MB=32
# One dynasty: most tables, and the size of all its tables together (MB).
#NCAA_DYNASTY_MAX_TABLES=200
#NCAA_DYNASTY_TABLES_MB=128
# One member who is not the commissioner: most tables of their own in one dynasty, and the size of all their own
# tables in every dynasty together (MB).
#NCAA_MEMBER_MAX_TABLES=100
#NCAA_MEMBER_TABLES_MB=64
# One dynasty's entry in dynasties.json (KB). A normal one is about 45.
#NCAA_DYNASTY_RECORD_KB=4096
# One uploaded game (KB; a normal one is about 40), and how many uploaded games one dynasty may keep.
#NCAA_GAME_DATA_MAX_KB=2048
#NCAA_DYNASTY_MAX_GAME_FILES=1000

# ---- optional: logging -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1 = also print decoded packet bodies (for debugging; credentials and passwords stay hidden). Very noisy.
#NCAA_LOG_BODIES=0
# on = also write private/capture-<time>.jsonl. Grows without limit: leave off on a server.
#NCAA_CAPTURE=off
